---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { brand } from "../config/brand";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How 3Stone AI collects, uses, protects, and deletes information across its website and products."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container section-narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</span>
      <h1>What happens to your information</h1>
      <p>Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long" })}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container section-narrow">
      <h2>Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        3Stone AI collects information you choose to provide, such as your
        name, email address, organization, account details, workspace content,
        uploaded files, and messages sent through our contact or product
        experiences. We use this information to provide, secure, support, and
        improve the services you request.
      </p>
      <p>
        The public website does not use advertising cookies. Its contact form
        opens your email client with your inquiry pre-filled and sends it to
        {" "}{brand.contactEmail} when you choose to send it.
      </p>

      <h2>Connected services</h2>
      <p>
        If you connect a third-party service, 3Stone AI accesses only the data
        and permissions needed for the features you activate. You can revoke
        access from the connected service or disconnect it within 3Stone One.
        Available integrations may vary by product edition.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Google, users select Drive files through Google Picker using the
        limited <code>drive.file</code> permission. Calendar access is
        read-only. Gmail access is limited to sending a message that the user
        composes and expressly chooses to send; 3Stone AI does not request
        access to read the user's Gmail inbox.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Microsoft, authorized features may access the signed-in user's
        Outlook mail and calendar, OneDrive files, mailbox settings, and Teams
        meetings, depending on the edition and permissions the user approves.
        Canvas connections may access the courses, assignments, and files the
        user authorizes through their institution.
      </p>

      <h2>How information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Connected data is used only to deliver user-facing functions such as
        displaying authorized files, email, events, assignments, and meetings;
        preparing requested summaries or assistance; and carrying out actions
        the user initiates. We do not sell personal information, use connected
        data for advertising, or provide it to data brokers.
      </p>

      <h2>Google API Services User Data</h2>
      <p>
        3Stone AI's use and transfer to any other app of information received
        from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data
        Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Workspace API data, including raw data and data derived from it,
        is not used to develop, improve, or train generalized artificial
        intelligence or machine-learning models. It is not transferred to a
        third-party AI provider for generalized model training. When a user
        requests an AI-assisted action, only the information needed to fulfill
        that request is processed for that user's personalized experience.
      </p>

      <h2>Protection and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We use HTTPS, least-privilege permissions, access controls, and
        workspace separation to protect information. Integration credentials
        and refresh tokens are encrypted at rest. Authorized service providers
        may process limited information on our behalf to host, secure, and
        operate the platform, subject to contractual and confidentiality
        obligations. We may also disclose information when required by law or
        to protect users and the service.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention, deletion, and user controls</h2>
      <p>
        We retain account and workspace information only for as long as needed
        to provide the service, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes, and
        maintain security. Connected-provider data is generally retrieved when
        needed; selected metadata and user-created workspace content may be
        retained so the requested feature continues to work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Disconnecting an integration revokes the connection and removes the
        stored credentials used by 3Stone AI. Users may also delete content
        through available product controls or request account and personal-data
        deletion by contacting us. Residual encrypted backups, when applicable,
        are removed through our normal backup lifecycle unless longer retention
        is legally required.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Our services rely on infrastructure and integration providers such as
        Vercel, Supabase, Google, Microsoft, and participating institutions.
        Those providers may process standard technical information under their
        own privacy terms when you use their services or authorize a connection.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and deletion requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this policy, contact us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .page-hero .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -1px;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .page-hero p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .section {
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-3xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .section-narrow {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-sm);
  }

  h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .section p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .section a {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
  }
</style>
